;; What this case exercises; edit by hand.  `bb corpus-accept' leaves it alone.
(:book "Teaching Programming Languages in a Post-Linnaean Age"
 :source "Teaching Programming Languages in a Post-Linnaean Age.pdf"
 :page 2
 :exercises "Bold section-head pairs a hair under the height gate, on a
3-page paper the support constant can never see.

Every section head is two records on one baseline - \"2.\" and
\"Students as Language Designers\" - one bold font
(NimbusRomNo9L-Medi) that the body never uses, gap ~4.6 modal
spaces, set at 1.10 body heights.  Denotational's same shape ran
1.23 body and joined; here the bare-number join refuses at its 1.15
height gate, so four heads reach the reader as a stranded enumerator
over a plain prose line.  The face is the signal the gate ignores:
a bold same-font pair in a non-body face joins at any height.

The paper has no outline and 3 pages, so the head style
(0.0128 Medi bold, every page) can never reach the 5-page support
constant either - the Academia Letters residual verbatim.  Support
scaled to document length promotes the joined heads, and the
whole-line-bold emphasis skip stops mattering: the heads are org
headings, styled as structure."
 :budget (:mid-sentence 0))
